meta {
  name: Space Create Record
  type: http
  seq: 140
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.createRecord
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "space": "at://did:plc:authorityaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa/space/org.example.bucket/main",
    "repo": {{did}},
    "collection": "org.example.note",
    "record": {
      "$type": "org.example.note",
      "text": "Hello from a permissioned space"
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Atproto Spaces: create a record in the authenticated account's permissioned repo
  within a space. "space" is a space ref — at://{authorityDid}/space/{spaceType}/{skey} —
  and "repo" MUST be the authenticated account's own DID (403 otherwise).

  The first write into a space this PDS has not seen records it, so a member can join a
  foreign authority's space with no prior setup. Writing into a space the operator has
  deleted returns 400 SpaceNotFound.

  Optional "rkey" (a TID is generated when absent) and "validate" (same semantics as
  com.atproto.repo.createRecord). The response "uri" is the full space record URI:
  {space}/{authorDid}/{collection}/{rkey}.

  Errors: 400 RecordAlreadyExists if the path is taken (use putRecord), 400 SpaceNotFound,
  403 InsufficientScope when the OAuth grant carries no covering "space:" token.
}
